>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `del_looper`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.del_looper : string -> simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Removes a named looper from an extension simpset.

`del_looper name ss` removes the looper `name` added by `add_looper`,
`set_looper` or `looper_ss`. Split loopers are removed with `del_split`.

### Failure

Never fails. If there is no looper `name`, a warning is printed and `ss`
is returned.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpExtLib.add_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
     (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss);
>>_ val ss' = simpExtLib.del_looper "conj" ss;
```

### See also

[`simpExtLib.add_looper`](#simpExtLib.add_looper),
[`simpExtLib.del_split`](#simpExtLib.del_split).
